From: Matt
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a4xx: timeout the A430 power-on poll (7.3 bring-up)

a4xx_pm_resume() polls RBBM_POWER_STATUS until the GPU reports powered
on, with no timeout. On the OnePlus 2 (kernel 7.3 bring-up) the GPU did
not come up on the first runtime resume, the read hung the bus and the
NMI watchdog took the kernel down ("Hard LOCKUP"). Give the poll a
500 ms timeout and fail the resume with -ETIMEDOUT instead, so a
power-on failure is a clean error instead of a hard lockup.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a4xx_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a4xx_gpu.c
@@ -579,11 +579,25 @@
 
 	if (adreno_is_a430(adreno_gpu)) {
 		unsigned int reg;
+		int timeout = 100000; /* 100000 * 5 us = 500 ms */
 		/* Set the default register values; set SW_COLLAPSE to 0 */
 		gpu_write(gpu, REG_A4XX_RBBM_POWER_CNTL_IP, 0x778000);
 		do {
 			udelay(5);
 			reg = gpu_read(gpu, REG_A4XX_RBBM_POWER_STATUS);
+			if (!--timeout) {
+				/*
+				 * OnePlus 2 (7.3 bring-up): this poll had no
+				 * timeout, so a GPU that never powered on hung
+				 * the CPU in the read and took the whole kernel
+				 * down with a hard lockup. Fail the resume
+				 * instead.
+				 */
+				dev_err(&gpu->pdev->dev,
+					"A430 GPU power-on timed out (RBBM_POWER_STATUS=%08x)\n",
+					reg);
+				return -ETIMEDOUT;
+			}
 		} while (!(reg & A4XX_RBBM_POWER_CNTL_IP_SP_TP_PWR_ON));
 	}
 	return 0;
